msgid ""
"要做具体的性能分析，profiling要开启**level1**，否则算子的关键信息会缺失。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"To perform detailed performance analysis, enable **level1** profiling; otherwise, key operator information will be missing.\n"
""

msgid ""
"### 1.host bound诊断\n"
""
msgstr ""
"### 1.host bound diagnosis\n"
""

msgid ""
"host bound是指CPU任务量总和大于NPU，导致NPU执行出现空泡的现象。可以通过看Host2Device的同步连线来判断，如果连线都是歪的，那证明这里的set信号早于wait信号，NPU一ready就执行了，那也是device bound：\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Host bound refers to the phenomenon where the total CPU workload exceeds that of the NPU, causing bubbles in NPU execution. You can determine this by examining the Host2Device synchronization lines. If the lines are skewed, it indicates that the set signal arrives before the wait signal, and the NPU executes as soon as it is ready. That is also device bound:\n"
""

msgid ""
"如果确诊为host bound，那么我们可以打开CPU侧，找出各算子的下发耗时。注意找的时候需要找出所有CPU耗时的累加值，而不能找单层，因为首次调用的耗时是很长的。例如下图的GmmSwigluQuant，CPU上首次调用需要1ms，后续每次只需要200μs。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"If it is diagnosed as host bound, you can enable the CPU side to find the dispatch time of each operator. Note that you need to find the accumulated value of all CPU time instead of a single layer. This is because the first call takes a long time. For example, for GmmSwigluQuant in the following figure, the first call on the CPU takes 1 ms. Subsequent calls only take 200 μs each.\n"
""

msgid ""
"此时有的算子在负重前行，有的算子拖了后腿，后者多于了前者。我们优先**找出来host耗时大于device的top算子，这些算子是拖后腿的**，可以交予算子团队重点分析。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"At this point, some operators carry the heavy workload, while others drag down the performance. The latter outnumber the former. Prioritize **finding the top operators where the host time is greater than the device time. These operators are dragging down the performance**, and you can assign them to the operator team for focused analysis.\n"
""

msgid ""
"### 2.组网合理性分析\n"
""
msgstr ""
"### 2. Networking Rationality Analysis\n"
""

msgid ""
"有的时候，模型组网没有按照最高效的方式来，这一点在profiling中是非常易于识别的，下面会介绍一下分析思路并给出例子。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Sometimes, the model networking is not implemented in the most efficient way. This is easy to identify in profiling. The following section introduces the analysis approach and provides examples.\n"
""

msgid ""
"通常来讲，LLM中的大的热点算子是Attention和FFN中的矩阵乘计算，二者加起来在prefill下可能达到计算耗时的70%+，decode下可能达到50%+。如果整体的耗时比例不符合预期，或者profiling中出现了一些新面孔，或者拼接类算子太多了，这都值得我们去分析一下模型组网，是不是使用算子的方式错了？尤其是拼接类算子，是值得我们逐一分析的。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Generally, the major hot spot operators in large language models (LLMs) are the matrix multiplication calculations in Attention and FFN. Together, they can account for over 70% of the computation time during prefill and over 50% during decode. If the overall time proportion does not meet expectations, new operators appear in the profiling, or there are too many concatenation operators, analyze the model network architecture. Determine whether the operators are used incorrectly. Concatenation operators in particular are worth analyzing individually.\n"
""

msgid ""
"对于slice/split/concat这样的拼接类算子，还有transpose/cast这种转换算子，他们的存在往往是前后算子不直接配套造成的。如果前一个算子可以直接对输出做好尾处理，往往可以节省一个算子的启动开销和一次冗余读写。但这样的改变不一定符合算子的基本设计原则。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Concatenation operators like slice/split/concat and conversion operators like transpose/cast often exist because the preceding and following operators do not directly match. If the preceding operator can directly perform tail processing on the output, it often saves an operator's startup overhead and a redundant read/write. However, such a change does not necessarily comply with the basic design principles of operators.\n"
""

msgid ""
"举一个正例，对于某次Matmul的输出shape为[m, n0 + n1]，在这后面我们接了两个slice，输入均为这个[m, n0 + n1]的tensor，输出分别为[m, n0]和[m, n1]。第一个优化的思路是将两个slice改为一个split，这样耗时可以基本减半，[m, n0 + n1]的显存也可以尽早释放。进一步优化的思路是将矩阵乘的权重从[k, n0 + n1]分割为[k, n0]和[k, n1]，将原来的矩阵乘任务分成两个（前提是这两个的耗时加起来不比之前的劣化太多，分核策略不能出问题），从而彻底消除这个slice/split操作。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Here is a positive example. The output shape of a Matmul is [m, n0 + n1]. After this, we connect two slice operations, both taking this [m, n0 + n1] tensor as input, with outputs [m, n0] and [m, n1] respectively. The first optimization idea is to replace the two slice operations with a single split. This roughly halves the execution time, and the device memory for [m, n0 + n1] can be released earlier. A further optimization is to split the matrix multiplication weights from [k, n0 + n1] into [k, n0] and [k, n1], dividing the original matrix multiplication task into two. This completely eliminates the slice/split operation. The prerequisite is that the combined execution time of the two does not degrade too much compared to the original, and the core allocation strategy must not break.\n"
""

msgid ""
"举一个反例，Rmsnorm(fp16)+Cast(fp16->fp32)+Matmul(fp32)，Rmsnorm虽然输入输出都是fp16，但考虑到累加运算的精度，内部是fp32做计算的。如果将Cast融到Rmsnorm内，本就内部使用fp32做计算的Rmsnorm就可以省去一个末尾fp32->fp16的cast，加上我们干掉的Cast，总共节省两个cast的同时避免了一次精度丢失。虽然这样看起来精度性能双收了，但fp16进，fp32出的Rmsnorm是反原则的（核心输入和输出需要是同数据类型），除非我们能在广大开源模型中频繁找到这样的结构，证明它的普适性，否则算子团队是不允许做这样的算子的。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Consider a counterexample: Rmsnorm(fp16)+Cast(fp16->fp32)+Matmul(fp32). Although the input and output of Rmsnorm are both fp16, it uses fp32 for internal calculations to ensure accumulation precision. If you fuse Cast into Rmsnorm, Rmsnorm can omit a final fp32->fp16 cast because it already uses fp32 for internal calculations. Together with the removed Cast, this saves two casts and avoids one precision loss. Although this seems to improve both precision and performance, an Rmsnorm that takes fp16 as input and outputs fp32 violates the principle. The core input and output must be the same data type. Unless you can frequently find such structures in open-source models to prove their general applicability, the operator team does not allow creating such operators.\n"
""

msgid ""
"### 3.算子性能初诊\n"
""
msgstr ""
"### 3. Preliminary diagnosis of operator performance\n"
""

msgid ""
"需要利用 `\"./ASCEND_PROFILER_OUTPUT/operator_details.csv\"`来做分析，从而判断算子是否有性能问题。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Analyze the `\"./ASCEND_PROFILER_OUTPUT/operator_details.csv\"` file to determine whether the operator has performance issues.\n"
""

msgid ""
"Profiling工具会统计这些流水线在不同核上的平均繁忙时间（xxx_time），与最慢核的完整kernel耗时（task_duration）做除法，得到流水线利用率（xxx_ratio）。这些流水线之间虽然互有依赖，且搬运类流水线会互抢带宽，但算子只要设计得当，是可以做到互相掩盖的。因此我们可以初步认为，**当算子的执行耗时大到一定程度上，算子应当在某一条流水线上形成bound**，即利用率要高到一定程度。经验上，在单算子耗时达到50μs时，就可以认为算子应当在bound流水线上，达成80%+的占用率了。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"The Profiling tool calculates the average busy time (xxx_time) of these pipelines across different cores. It divides this value by the complete kernel duration (task_duration) of the slowest core to obtain the pipeline utilization (xxx_ratio). Although these pipelines depend on each other and the data transfer pipelines compete for bandwidth, operators can be designed to overlap with each other. Therefore, we can preliminarily conclude that **when the execution duration of an operator reaches a certain threshold, the operator should form a bound on one pipeline**, that is, the utilization should reach a sufficiently high level. Empirically, when the duration of a single operator reaches 50μs, the operator can be considered to be on the bound pipeline, achieving a utilization of 80% or higher.\n"
""

msgid ""
"以下图为例，第一行是一个FA算子，第二行是一个Matmul算子，FA在vec流水线上达到了88.1%的利用率，Matmul算子在mac流水线上达到了89.8%的利用率，他们的性能可以认为是合格的。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Take the following figure as an example. The first row is an FA operator, and the second row is a Matmul operator. The FA operator achieves a utilization rate of 88.1% on the vec pipeline. The Matmul operator achieves a utilization rate of 89.8% on the mac pipeline. Their performance is considered acceptable.\n"
""

msgid ""
"### 4.亲和shape调整\n"
""
msgstr ""
"### 4. Affinity shape adjustment\n"
""

msgid ""
"对于一个模型而言，超参是我们控制不了的，但我们可以控制并发度、权重格式、切分策略等因素来迎合算子，使其发挥出最大的性能，这一节主要从算子搬运效率和负载均衡两个方面出发，讨论模型侧值得尝试的调整方向。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"For a model, you cannot control hyperparameters. However, you can control factors such as concurrency, weight format, and partitioning strategy to accommodate operators and maximize their performance. This section discusses adjustment directions worth trying on the model side, focusing on two aspects: operator transfer efficiency and load balancing.\n"
""

msgid ""
"#### 4.1 搬运效率亲和的shape\n"
""
msgstr ""
"#### 4.1 Data movement efficiency-friendly shapes\n"
""

msgid ""
"mte2是一个自身效率严重受shape影响的流水线。要想让mte2保证最大搬运效率，我们需要保障如下两个条件至少满足其一：\n"
""
msgstr ""
"mte2 is a pipeline whose efficiency is heavily affected by shape. To ensure that mte2 achieves maximum data transfer efficiency, ensure that at least one of the following two conditions is met:\n"
""

msgid ""
"**（1）被搬运的矩阵使用nz作为format（最优）\n"
"（2）被搬运的矩阵的尾轴512B对齐，且不为16KB的整数倍（近似最优）**\n"
""
msgstr ""
"**(1) The matrix being moved uses nz as the format (optimal)\n"
"(2) The trailing axis of the matrix being moved is aligned to 512B and is not an integer multiple of 16KB (approximately optimal)**\n"
""

msgid ""
"对于权重矩阵来说，推理阶段尤其是decode，我们通常满足（1），训练阶段我们通常满足（2）。**如果我们做不到（1），我们就要迎合（2）**。典型的手段有：\n"
""
msgstr ""
"For weight matrices, during the inference phase, especially decode, we typically satisfy (1), and during the training phase, we typically satisfy (2). **If we cannot achieve (1), we must accommodate (2)**. Typical approaches include:\n"
""

msgid ""
"1、如果没达成（1），矩阵的首轴是亲和的而尾轴不亲和，那么对它做transpose\n"
"2、调整TP切分策略，避免出现不亲和的尾轴\n"
""
msgstr ""
"1、If condition (1) is not met, and the leading axis of the matrix is affinitive but the trailing axis is not, transpose it.\n"
"2、Adjust the TP splitting strategy to avoid non-affinitive trailing axes.\n"
""

msgid ""
"#### 4.2 负载均衡亲和的shape\n"
""
msgstr ""
"#### 4.2 Load balancing affinity shape\n"
""

msgid ""
"在算子shape不大时，受制于算子语义，我们有可能不能把所有核都利用起来，或者即使开满核，负载均衡却很差。这一小节主要是对decode阶段的小shape做分析。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"When the operator shape changes, due to operator semantics, you may not be able to utilize all cores. Even if all cores are enabled, the load balancing may be poor. This subsection mainly analyzes small shapes in the decode phase.\n"
""

msgid ""
"首先，我们明确出当前NPU卡是多少核的，如果不清楚，跑出来的profiling里都是20、40这样的数，就说明是20核，反之是24核。这里我的24核其实是代表了一个cube和两个vector组成的小组，我们可以认为是一个cube作为主核，带了两个vector作为从核。如果一个算子是纯vector算子，那么就不再有组的概念，40或48个vector核会作为主核直接独立去拿逻辑任务。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"First, determine the number of cores on the current NPU card. If you are unsure, check the profiling results. If the numbers are 20 or 40, the card has 20 cores. Otherwise, it has 24 cores. The 24 cores here actually represent a group consisting of one cube and two vectors. You can consider one cube as the primary core, with two vectors as secondary cores. If an operator is a pure vector operator, the concept of groups no longer applies. The 40 or 48 vector cores act as primary cores and independently fetch logical tasks.\n"
""

msgid ""
"对于LLM中的vector算子，它的一种常见分核策略有可能是分在最高维，也就是batch维，常见于对低维（也叫尾轴）有规约操作的norm类、动态量化类等算子；另一种是整体拍平，允许算子切分得非常细的算子，如elementwise算子。对于第一种，我们就可以在模型侧关注它的负载均衡问题。例如我们打48batch，而硬件却是个40个vector核，那这40个核会循环2次，第二次有多数的核会无事可做，这个batch数就可以认为是不友好的。如果将batch打到64或80，性能可以预见会是无损的。同样的情况下，如果是48核的卡，那我们可以认为这就是个非常友好的batch数。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"For vector operators in a large language model (LLM), one common core partitioning strategy is to partition along the highest dimension, that is, the batch dimension. This is common for operators that perform reduction operations on lower dimensions (also known as the tail axis), such as norm operators and dynamic quantization operators. Another strategy is to flatten the entire tensor, which allows operators to be split very finely, such as elementwise operators. For the first strategy, you can focus on its load balancing issue on the model side. For example, if you set the batch size to 48 but the hardware has 40 vector cores, these 40 cores will loop twice. During the second loop, most cores will have nothing to do. This batch size can be considered unfriendly. If you set the batch size to 64 or 80, the performance is expected to be lossless. In the same situation, if the card has 48 cores, you can consider this a very friendly batch size.\n"
""

msgid ""
"对于cube类算子，它常见的分核策略是以base快去切分M和N（K轴是累加轴，对它分核会引入确定性问题）。最常见的分块是baseM=128，baseN=256。在decode阶段，我们的耗时基本可以看做都是在搬权重，这是因为激活的M极小，M方向大概率只分了一块，那么右矩阵就只需要搬一次。所以我们在M≤128的范围内可以尽情提高M，对性能都基本是无损的，如果M大于128，可以认为(128, 256]是下一个性能分档。\n"
"除了M外，N轴切分的任务也影响算子亲和性，以deepseekR1中的MLA预处理为例，它会使用同一个激活（shape为[batch_size, 7168]）与两个权重做矩阵乘(shape为[7168, 1536]和[7168, 576])。在batch_size打不大的情况下，即使baseN缩短为128，N轴都不能用满核数，所以此时这两个矩阵乘各自的耗时，会约等于将他们权重N轴拼起来乘(shape为[7168, 2112])的矩阵乘的耗时。如果仅考虑模型竞争力，我们更希望对这两个权重做合并，否则两个小的矩阵乘带宽利用率都会非常差。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"For cube operators, a common core partitioning strategy is to split the M and N axes using base blocks (the K axis is the accumulation axis, and partitioning it across cores introduces determinism issues). The most common block sizes are baseM=128 and baseN=256. During the decode phase, the time consumption is essentially all spent moving weights. This is because the M dimension of the activation is extremely small, and the M direction likely has only one block, so the right matrix only needs to be moved once. Therefore, within the range of M≤128, you can freely increase M, which is essentially lossless for performance. If M is greater than 128, you can consider (128, 256] as the next performance tier.\n"
"\n"
"Besides M, the task of splitting the N axis also affects operator affinity. For example, the MLA preprocessing in deepseekR1 uses the same activation (with a shape of [batch_size, 7168]) to perform matrix multiplication with two weights (with shapes of [7168, 1536] and [7168, 576]). When the batch_size is not large, even if baseN is reduced to 128, the N axis cannot fully utilize all cores. Therefore, the time consumption of each of these two matrix multiplications is approximately equal to the time consumption of a single matrix multiplication with their weight N axes concatenated (with a shape of [7168, 2112]). If you only consider model competitiveness, we prefer to merge these two weights; otherwise, the bandwidth utilization of both small matrix multiplications will be very poor.\n"
""

msgid ""
"对于Attention算子，它常见的分核策略是q_seqlen、batch_size和kv_headnum。增量阶段q_seqlen会以MTP和GQA倍数做合并，但是通常也不会大过128，划分不出第二个任务，那么并行度基本就是batch_size * kv_headnum。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"For the Attention operator, the common core partitioning strategy uses q_seqlen, batch_size, and kv_headnum. In the incremental phase, q_seqlen is merged using the MTP and GQA multiples, but it usually does not exceed 128. Therefore, it cannot be split into a second task, and the parallelism is basically batch_size * kv_headnum.\n"
""

msgid ""
"总的来说，我们可以依据shape信息和算子类别，对算子是否有负载均衡问题作出识别，从而对我们切分策略选择，最高吞吐量的batch策略作出预判。\n"
""
msgstr ""
"Overall, you can identify whether an operator has a load balancing problem based on shape information and operator categories. This helps you predict the split strategy selection and the batch strategy for maximum throughput.\n"
""
